#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128852 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6506f7e3-4c69-5352-a09d-262adee65e59" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9267ebc3-36a0-58d3-85ab-2687e21151c0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4048" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $y = \\cot\\left(2x-\\dfrac\\pi 6\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "Given a function of the form\n\n$$\ny = A\\cot(Bx +C) + D\n$$\n\nthe period is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\pi}{B}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=2$. Therefore, the period is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128853 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "100740e1-a959-53aa-af58-034a2fc16a8c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4049" :question/problem "Which expression gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x) = \\cot \\left(2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6\\right)$?" :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\cot x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\cot \\left(2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6\\right)\n$$\n\nwe replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with\n\n$$\n\\left(2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6\\right)\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n$$\n\nSolving for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + \\frac{π}{6} &= \\frac{π}{2} + nπ \\\\\n2x &= \\frac{π}{2} + nπ - \\frac{π}{6} \\\\\n2x &= \\frac{π}{3} + nπ \\\\\nx &= \\frac{π}{6} + \\frac{nπ}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} + \\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128854 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Asymptotes of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c2431212-e58e-52fe-a00b-6f9abfa3589d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4050" :question/problem "What expression gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\tan\\left(2x\\right)$?" :question/worked-solution "The asymptotes of $y=\\tan x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n \\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(2x\\right)\n$$\n\nwe replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $2x$. This gives\n\n$$\n2x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n$$\n\nSolving for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x &= \\frac{π}{2} + nπ \\\\\nx &= \\frac{π}{4} + \\frac{nπ}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is\n\n$$\nx= \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + \\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128855 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Domain of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8faa2f76-decb-545b-b47e-0c37725a34dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4051" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $y=\\tan\\left(\\dfrac x 2\\right)$?" :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\tan x$ is given by the expression\n\n$$\nx \\neq \\dfrac\\pi 2 + n\\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(\\dfrac x 2\\right)\n$$\n\nwe replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac x 2\\right)\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac x 2 \\neq \\dfrac\\pi 2 + n\\pi\n$$\n\nSolving for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{x}{2} & \\ne \\frac{π}{2} + nπ \\\\ x & \\ne π + 2nπ\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is\n\n$$\nx \\neq \\pi + 2n\\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6506f7e3-4c69-5352-a09d-262adee65e59" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fbd2b10-bf8f-57cd-9e65-a4395d7fb704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251946} {:answer/id #uuid "52ad0875-0cf4-5915-b999-5b7e32707cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251947} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfc8589-055b-5883-b07d-f2af8a48a333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251948} {:answer/id #uuid "d2568bf0-a54e-5c14-be24-a51304a31739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251949} {:answer/id #uuid "61950bbc-adec-5f03-82a9-21679126b907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2568bf0-a54e-5c14-be24-a51304a31739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251949} :answer-field/id #uuid "6173397b-30f2-5d92-84f5-d9dd6f10cdce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251945}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01426a8e-7412-5606-9f96-998be83dbedb" :question/math-academy-id "q-117658" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9x+2\\pi }{3})+4.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9x+2\\pi }{3})+4=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=3,$ and so the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6506f7e3-4c69-5352-a09d-262adee65e59" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "854e3ba5-4537-593f-8493-3255fafd9209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251953} {:answer/id #uuid "5f048b93-a37f-5185-8f6f-c990463d533e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251954} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c0139b-7dc5-5761-86ef-3f9807c9fdfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251955} {:answer/id #uuid "be9981c4-cdce-5453-9d54-ed0d6858ac69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251956} {:answer/id #uuid "0b3294cd-dd92-551a-a90d-d2e7d1100e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6c0139b-7dc5-5761-86ef-3f9807c9fdfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251955} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3d3fa3-34dd-5541-8642-aec4341d5912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251952}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7197633-1dbe-55f1-95bb-938aa5e3cbd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-117659" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)+6.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=3.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6506f7e3-4c69-5352-a09d-262adee65e59" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f69c12-a61a-5a6e-83fa-c21d944cb90a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251960} {:answer/id #uuid "c5554f8a-aa45-5ae5-9a7b-741f6811666b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251961} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f32612-83c6-5f3f-acb1-90bb53b2b942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251962} {:answer/id #uuid "181fc49e-b4e2-51dc-9ae1-9fc05e8f98d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251963} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5519de-28e6-590e-b9f2-e3272158cc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0f32612-83c6-5f3f-acb1-90bb53b2b942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251962} :answer-field/id #uuid "cffb71dc-66d9-54a9-97e7-81675140cfc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251959}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98e0e2a3-3be6-538a-ab1e-66e87a34ff82" :question/math-academy-id "q-117661" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{8x-\\pi }{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that\n\n$$\nf(x)=-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{8x-\\pi }{4})=-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=2,$ and so the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd6a47b0-70f8-5535-91bc-f37d35f31daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251967} {:answer/id #uuid "9cfca77a-46d9-5a9a-abfd-8f0a756dd206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251968} {:answer/id #uuid "0b7254f5-1d63-5878-9cfb-9f334bc87dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251969} {:answer/id #uuid "3c65af0b-b5f1-5b72-a2b0-90f29d5c40fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251970} {:answer/id #uuid "93450cc6-63e0-5676-8344-8f81d2d5c438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93450cc6-63e0-5676-8344-8f81d2d5c438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251971} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c42ceb1-23a1-5acb-8615-0e4d492ed9f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251966}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "931f4a51-06bf-59f0-b68f-290dcf1cfb73" :question/math-academy-id "q-117670" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & =n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =4n\\pi +\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7eaad2bb-6739-5a3b-a0f0-ff63413cf5f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251974} {:answer/id #uuid "bc0ab833-15ec-5a78-b98e-b0a5ebc8cd87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251975} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fd5faa-3ff6-5d33-80f0-4b28ae9e41a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251976} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b05473-bcc5-54a5-b454-e7bc84e3a9d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251977} {:answer/id #uuid "fc468c49-1e06-5072-93d6-5eb8051c62ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0b05473-bcc5-54a5-b454-e7bc84e3a9d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251977} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ec4258-e789-553b-ba87-3b0438148bab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251973}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ac30df1-20ef-5dc8-9420-e3dd6c1ddd9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-117671" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+\\pi )?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+\\pi ),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x+\\pi ).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x+\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Asymptotes of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7705ae8-ff65-5b25-a3c2-a141bb759b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251981} {:answer/id #uuid "48c1651b-0d9d-56de-a79a-341d8e5ee39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251982} {:answer/id #uuid "0dd651f3-7ebf-5ba4-a959-178b97dcc31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251983} {:answer/id #uuid "a24f6cbe-39ac-563a-af3a-b1f48c70bbf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251984} {:answer/id #uuid "ac6b69f4-d51c-589c-bbf6-ca6e40118d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac6b69f4-d51c-589c-bbf6-ca6e40118d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251985} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbfd00ec-aab3-5c84-a0f4-d752e0c5c1ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251980}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21c3d7aa-d5c5-5b6d-84ac-78dece1c964e" :question/math-academy-id "q-117698" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Asymptotes of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc670b1b-974b-513e-8be0-d9e84a7a5726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}+2n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251988} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf8e401-5c59-599b-841a-40f398a00484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{2}+n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251989} {:answer/id #uuid "67d1cb7c-9e33-54e9-b715-bda925d62520" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{2}+3n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251990} {:answer/id #uuid "3717a920-083f-5461-bd5c-b35755bc02f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}+n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251991} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc197b0-09a5-5d38-a900-241aa9db002c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}+3n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dc197b0-09a5-5d38-a900-241aa9db002c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}+3n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251992} :answer-field/id #uuid "0500ba32-0540-56ae-8ff0-4bc1001ca67e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251987}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94a88f64-34b6-5bf0-b22d-e438ec352322" :question/math-academy-id "q-117700" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function  $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{\\pi x}{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}+3n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}+3n,$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Domain of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5043461f-8bce-50ef-b578-6ca634088c06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne 2\\pi +2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251995} {:answer/id #uuid "a7966234-1759-5903-b572-f252f5b17e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251996} {:answer/id #uuid "dd903620-1101-5e99-9c45-b1688d5b2871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\pi +4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251997} {:answer/id #uuid "9165c59d-76f8-521f-aa12-908691e923b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251998} {:answer/id #uuid "8edbf9eb-0ba5-564a-a68a-bca1fc18bab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne 2\\pi +4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8edbf9eb-0ba5-564a-a68a-bca1fc18bab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne 2\\pi +4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251999} :answer-field/id #uuid "1edcc6a4-58fb-5763-ba6e-506139a7deb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251994}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "717d3db3-4268-5678-8f9b-8e1177d7e4db" :question/math-academy-id "q-117707" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function  $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\ne n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} & \\ne n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2\\pi +4n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne 2\\pi +4n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Domain of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97b51fac-9041-540f-bf00-61b49f0fb809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252002} {:answer/id #uuid "590c090f-f1db-50c4-a7ba-9fb1e893b63b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252003} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d76b06-2577-59d3-89ac-05aa2a528fe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252004} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6142be-1b3a-5b3f-9623-57292bac7905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252005} {:answer/id #uuid "fff16a5a-dbae-54d5-9be5-61c6afc8a93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "590c090f-f1db-50c4-a7ba-9fb1e893b63b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252003} :answer-field/id #uuid "4839406e-b3d3-573b-a8e2-1bbe065148aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252001}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ddd543ad-2469-5e25-9a6e-88a7c29db10a" :question/math-academy-id "q-117708" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x)+2?$  Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x)+2,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(5x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n5x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2\\cdot 5}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Domain of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b4a323a-189d-5e8e-857e-5656b2bb2133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{8}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252009} {:answer/id #uuid "90725073-791b-5b91-9393-e3fa206d7074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252010} {:answer/id #uuid "1f17f0d9-18a6-599b-8bdb-22f4798695b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252011} {:answer/id #uuid "19af612d-31ff-58de-a128-6f4d38f95bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252012} {:answer/id #uuid "b4011db1-95d9-5af6-ae58-1bdde7f1d011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f17f0d9-18a6-599b-8bdb-22f4798695b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252011} :answer-field/id #uuid "3855cdbd-e3f4-5825-87e0-b7c46ca54a6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252008}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d6d6740-e5dd-5281-92d1-875d6a4f4564" :question/math-academy-id "q-26063" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)?$  Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2\\cdot 2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Domain of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f91fa18f-cc26-5f7f-af1c-81c044da4cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252016} {:answer/id #uuid "be6ad5dc-720e-5d6b-9b5d-67d1945dcd6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252017} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfbb267-6c68-53fd-93d4-9a2c6abf6316" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{2\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252018} {:answer/id #uuid "0313897b-d082-5b0a-8473-054e34aaa182" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{5}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252019} {:answer/id #uuid "2180389c-16c2-53b5-844f-614c25473c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+5n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be6ad5dc-720e-5d6b-9b5d-67d1945dcd6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ne \\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252017} :answer-field/id #uuid "6647242e-d797-5eb9-9052-6f11d43d49ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7bb983e-87e4-57d6-84cd-bfae99f753e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-26245" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-1?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-1,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Asymptotes of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0432cfc9-68fb-5ad7-aa9e-7e5cf4bdb790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=n\\cdot {180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252023} {:answer/id #uuid "e6fa9e18-8dbc-5940-b827-7af2913efd21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252024} {:answer/id #uuid "2fecbb8b-1cd1-545c-9f15-7eb5277f8712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252025} {:answer/id #uuid "2f309a7a-17f6-5e7d-98b3-afffa62139ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252026} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c72aa2-6df8-5857-bcd6-f4c8f1702be2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f309a7a-17f6-5e7d-98b3-afffa62139ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252026} :answer-field/id #uuid "18d653d3-097d-5cce-911f-a8f0a2c0cfc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252022}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be415b89-7d30-5ce9-84ec-af79c6162caf" :question/math-academy-id "q-29349" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)-2,$ where $x$ is measured in degrees? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)-2,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x).$ This gives:\n\n$$\n2x={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSolving this for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a1c3a6-f55e-5f93-8bbf-7fa85cca7f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252030} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a569ac-e01a-5404-b0d5-522aac50fc77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252031} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e18aa0-c09d-5b4b-97ce-c19e7af05f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252032} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c6ed6a-af50-5b1e-b1e4-d40797ed45fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252033} {:answer/id #uuid "5dad872b-df87-51c0-b925-b40c9932c8b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03a1c3a6-f55e-5f93-8bbf-7fa85cca7f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252030} :answer-field/id #uuid "db5c04e6-fa51-5f0b-bebc-9277b9c7b956" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5982e3bf-c026-5567-a1c4-ad521afd020a" :question/math-academy-id "q-29556" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Domain of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad75ad68-30b1-577c-9ee8-2ff0cc