\\frac{\\pi }{6} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ 3x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot 3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{9}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6506f7e3-4c69-5352-a09d-262adee65e59" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94d1a1d0-6f1d-5d61-beec-659291a2cbaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252044} {:answer/id #uuid "2c19b484-dd08-53a9-87d0-b9615f967829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252045} {:answer/id #uuid "9056714c-48c5-51af-b752-9b1b2d1e7c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252046} {:answer/id #uuid "842f89cf-7456-5d0d-b656-d85d7194f794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252047} {:answer/id #uuid "3046d72b-f6ba-51da-a83b-0cddc2ea8460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3046d72b-f6ba-51da-a83b-0cddc2ea8460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252048} :answer-field/id #uuid "a88c4ece-5892-569c-8d3d-846440fc3371" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252043}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24dfd901-81c8-539f-94c6-3f7b3cb2aaed" :question/math-academy-id "q-65840" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=5.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6506f7e3-4c69-5352-a09d-262adee65e59" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f68b1cd8-6067-5501-8f92-6cee562d84c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252051} {:answer/id #uuid "c65b5e91-6eee-5d32-bf29-b51a2eb4676c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252052} {:answer/id #uuid "b3257ece-7489-56f0-9b5d-291aa3413a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252053} {:answer/id #uuid "af55ffa7-d897-508c-93ab-2f28024bfacb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252054} {:answer/id #uuid "3994d247-73bc-5405-81eb-1234ebd380b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af55ffa7-d897-508c-93ab-2f28024bfacb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252054} :answer-field/id #uuid "281204a1-0c57-5900-9fbe-092c3391c226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252050}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8c83dbb-9abd-54d7-a1da-99ab2a25d147" :question/math-academy-id "q-81541" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=7\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{1}{6}x-\\frac{\\pi }{12}).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{1}{6}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{1}{6})}=6\\pi .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c3ec7c5-948b-51c9-b48e-24d1d7642a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252058} {:answer/id #uuid "405dccb9-421f-5ca5-8a1a-e335223025c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252059} {:answer/id #uuid "00a8a0f7-6d80-51c9-aa3f-9b586b80325c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252060} {:answer/id #uuid "3bda0fb4-5685-5043-bf3f-25dda1f5dc09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252061} {:answer/id #uuid "5b126c27-830f-5961-a568-81f28560584a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}+4n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bda0fb4-5685-5043-bf3f-25dda1f5dc09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252061} :answer-field/id #uuid "956c1634-e434-5b82-bb05-a0324989e781" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252057}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93b12d9d-284c-5b30-95d3-e45daf65e800" :question/math-academy-id "q-81545" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(4x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n4x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a034fbd5-1026-518d-a2b3-4510c6e2140b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252065} {:answer/id #uuid "712173b1-8a83-54a8-be05-e824d52e6a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252066} {:answer/id #uuid "415c05d7-539b-5ac9-ab5a-4274f7b8114a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252067} {:answer/id #uuid "60a631aa-e611-5ae9-a5b0-5366dacb9b82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+6n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252068} {:answer/id #uuid "630459d3-f834-5441-a47b-795f9faf5c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+3n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "712173b1-8a83-54a8-be05-e824d52e6a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252066} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6ab3c17-f018-59d3-a1b9-88b7da567525" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252064}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a139c5ef-c768-5c96-ba0a-7b4e6441e50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81546" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 6x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{n\\pi }{6},$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Asymptotes of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d36b0e72-12fb-56da-9d69-aeab36465431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252072} {:answer/id #uuid "94a9c705-d918-5c04-8baf-f7fdc2febcc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}+n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252073} {:answer/id #uuid "2632ecad-99a0-5b25-b4c6-7b288365c4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}+2n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252074} {:answer/id #uuid "1378fb86-9fdb-5224-965b-0fd6baa7aac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252075} {:answer/id #uuid "344d6be3-4b53-578f-9a97-425fdfd60d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1378fb86-9fdb-5224-965b-0fd6baa7aac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252075} :answer-field/id #uuid "826f4f7e-d604-53a1-90e3-6fd5185bca03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252071}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d986496d-d5b7-54a7-bed8-4a67e7db20c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-81556" :question/problem "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function  $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\pi x)?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\pi x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\pi x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\pi x=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=n,$ where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Asymptotes of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e415958c-541c-5232-8d7d-38506dd11516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 1759